WEBVTT

00:00:07.637 --> 00:00:13.780
The Queen of New Orleans.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.071
Part 1.

00:00:15.131 --> 00:00:21.675
The Queen is Crown.

00:00:21.735 --> 00:00:31.300
New Orleans 1805.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:38.876
Two hundred years ago, New Orleans was quite a place to be.

00:00:38.936 --> 00:00:42.338
Lots of interest in people lived there or passed through.

00:00:42.398 --> 00:00:54.288
Musicians, gamblers, sailors, some nights the French Quarter of the city was, well let's say, it was lively.

00:00:54.348 --> 00:01:02.023
Down in Congo Square, all flats Congo is the people there called it.

00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:04.519
The scene was also pretty lively.

00:01:04.579 --> 00:01:07.676
It was a place where freed slaves used to go.

00:01:07.736 --> 00:01:10.858
A place where they worshipped a special kind of religion.

00:01:10.918 --> 00:01:13.791
This religion had a lot of different names.

00:01:13.851 --> 00:01:16.874
Akan, Ifa or Isha.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:21.168
Nowadays we call it voodoo.

00:01:21.228 --> 00:01:26.182
About that time, there was a voodoo queen in New Orleans.

00:01:26.242 --> 00:01:31.396
A name was Sanite Dede, and everyone was afraid of them.

00:01:31.456 --> 00:01:34.538
Lots of people used to ask her for favors.

00:01:34.598 --> 00:01:38.962
And she made a good living out of it.

00:01:39.022 --> 00:01:42.495
What do you want?

00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:44.176
I need your help.

00:01:44.236 --> 00:01:45.388
Oh yeah.

00:01:45.448 --> 00:01:48.780
I owe somebody a lot of money.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.362
I want to know if...

00:01:50.382 --> 00:01:52.944
You have anything that belongs to him.

00:01:53.004 --> 00:01:56.718
Yes, I managed to get this from him.

00:01:56.777 --> 00:01:58.891
Nice handkerchief.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.594
Yes, he must be pretty rich.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.215
Yes, he is.

00:02:03.275 --> 00:02:06.637
How much do you owe him?

00:02:06.697 --> 00:02:07.948
$5,000.

00:02:08.008 --> 00:02:11.119
Then you're one stupid son of a bitch.

00:02:11.179 --> 00:02:12.380
It wasn't my fault.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.082
This is gonna cost you money.

00:02:15.142 --> 00:02:16.802
I'll pay you what I can.

00:02:16.822 --> 00:02:18.083
You'll pay me $500.

00:02:18.143 --> 00:02:18.283
$500?

00:02:18.303 --> 00:02:18.763
I can't.

00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:19.054
$500.

00:02:19.114 --> 00:02:20.284
Take it or leave it.

00:02:20.304 --> 00:02:21.405
But I can't.

00:02:21.465 --> 00:02:25.456
Okay, goodbye.

00:02:25.516 --> 00:02:28.818
No!

00:02:28.878 --> 00:02:29.709
Open the door!

00:02:29.769 --> 00:02:30.980
Open the door!

00:02:31.039 --> 00:02:32.761
I'll pay you $500.

00:02:32.821 --> 00:02:39.706
Bring me half tomorrow.

00:02:39.766 --> 00:02:44.158
Sanite Dade was the number one voodoo woman in New Orleans.

00:02:44.218 --> 00:02:47.660
But then, someone else came along.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:55.034
This is the story of Marie LaVoe, the woman who became the new voodoo queen of New Orleans.

00:02:55.094 --> 00:03:01.164
At the beginning of our story, Marie was just a simple hairdresser.

00:03:01.224 --> 00:03:03.454
Marie?

00:03:03.514 --> 00:03:04.614
Marie?

00:03:04.674 --> 00:03:05.875
Hello Blanche.

00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:09.156
Marie, do you have time to cut my hair today?

00:03:09.216 --> 00:03:11.226
Not now Blanche, no.

00:03:11.286 --> 00:03:12.567
Maybe tomorrow?

00:03:12.627 --> 00:03:14.937
Okay, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:03:14.997 --> 00:03:15.708
Fine.

00:03:15.768 --> 00:03:18.892
Bye for now.

00:03:18.952 --> 00:03:22.246
Well, hello.

00:03:22.306 --> 00:03:23.786
Oh, my God.

00:03:23.846 --> 00:03:25.426
You frightened me.

00:03:25.486 --> 00:03:28.208
I can't see anything with the blinds down.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:29.088
Who is it?

00:03:29.148 --> 00:03:32.269
Well, Marie, don't you remember my voice?

00:03:32.329 --> 00:03:35.170
Jack, is it you?

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.061
Sure is.

00:03:38.121 --> 00:03:42.502
What do you think you're doing sitting here in the dark?

00:03:42.562 --> 00:03:43.723
What do you want?

00:03:43.783 --> 00:03:46.835
Marie, what do you think I want?

00:03:46.894 --> 00:03:48.756
I don't know, Jack.

00:03:48.816 --> 00:03:50.496
I'm not a mind-reader.

00:03:50.556 --> 00:03:51.947
Come on, Marie.

00:03:52.007 --> 00:03:54.678
Did you forget Friday night already?

00:03:54.738 --> 00:03:57.669
Friday night was Friday night, Jack.

00:03:57.729 --> 00:04:00.020
Today is another day.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:08.094
And today could be another day like Friday, Marie.

00:04:08.154 --> 00:04:17.264
There was quite a party the day that Marie LaVoe and Jack Paris got married.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:24.486
Maria LaVoe, fine looking woman, intelligent, and knew how to make an honest buck.

00:04:24.546 --> 00:04:35.066
Jack Paris, well, he was fine looking too, but, well, let's say he wasn't a regular kind of guy, you know?

00:04:35.126 --> 00:04:39.260
The kind that gets up in the morning and goes to work.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:44.884
If he was up in the morning, it was because he'd been up all night drinking and gambling.

00:04:44.944 --> 00:04:51.605
A lot of people were very surprised when Marie married someone like Jack.

00:04:51.664 --> 00:05:00.127
And do you, Marie, take Jack to be your lawful wedded husband?

00:05:00.187 --> 00:05:01.277
I do.

00:05:01.337 --> 00:05:09.249
And do you, Jack, take Marie to be your lawful wedded wife?

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.260
Jack?

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:12.934
Huh?

00:05:12.994 --> 00:05:20.743
Do you take this woman to be your lawful wedded wife?

00:05:20.803 --> 00:05:22.765
Sure, preacher man.

00:05:22.825 --> 00:05:25.527
Jack, just say I do.

00:05:25.587 --> 00:05:28.079
Okay, I do.

00:05:28.139 --> 00:05:30.871
Good, I now pronounce you man and wife.

00:05:30.931 --> 00:05:32.382
You may kiss the bride.

00:05:32.442 --> 00:05:33.884
It's all right, Mr. preacher.

00:05:33.904 --> 00:05:40.875
I already did that.

00:05:40.935 --> 00:05:47.816
Hey, Marie.

00:05:47.876 --> 00:05:49.037
Hi, Blanche.

00:05:49.097 --> 00:05:51.609
What's it like to be a married woman?

00:05:51.669 --> 00:05:55.692
When I find out, I'll tell you.

00:05:55.751 --> 00:05:59.694
Hello, Jack.

00:05:59.754 --> 00:06:01.676
Well, hello.

00:06:01.736 --> 00:06:04.187
Now, do I know you?

00:06:04.247 --> 00:06:05.948
You sure do.

00:06:06.008 --> 00:06:08.050
Refresh my memory, pretty lady.

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:09.511
My name is Gina.

00:06:09.571 --> 00:06:12.083
We met in Baton Rouge a year ago.

00:06:12.103 --> 00:06:13.395
Ah.

00:06:13.455 --> 00:06:17.228
Yes, very refreshing.

00:06:17.288 --> 00:06:21.391
So, Jack, you went and got yourself a wife.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:22.781
I sure did.

00:06:22.841 --> 00:06:26.593
Marion Marie LaVoe's the best thing I ever did.

00:06:26.653 --> 00:06:28.784
You think so?

00:06:28.844 --> 00:06:32.966
Well, now, you trying to tell me something?

00:06:33.026 --> 00:06:41.172
Well, yes I am, but here ain't the right place to tell you.

00:06:41.232 --> 00:06:45.116
Hurry.

00:06:45.176 --> 00:06:46.836
What is it, Blanche?

00:06:46.896 --> 00:06:49.148
I think you should go outside.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.959
Why should I do that, Blanche?

00:06:51.019 --> 00:06:53.100
I'm having a fine time here.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.160
Right.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:07:00.572
And Jack is having a fine time out the bank.

00:07:00.632 --> 00:07:06.113
Oh Jack, it's so good to see you again.

00:07:06.133 --> 00:07:07.475
This show is.

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:08.787
Come here.

00:07:08.846 --> 00:07:10.148
Not here.

00:07:10.208 --> 00:07:11.158
Where then?

00:07:11.218 --> 00:07:12.530
I have a room.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:16.094
Second floor in a rooming house on Rose Street.

00:07:16.154 --> 00:07:18.186
Number 21.

00:07:18.246 --> 00:07:21.059
Why don't you come and see me there?

00:07:21.119 --> 00:07:22.941
Show thing.

00:07:23.001 --> 00:07:25.144
There they are.

00:07:25.204 --> 00:07:26.646
Oh, my God.

00:07:26.706 --> 00:07:28.858
Jesus, how do I get out of here?

00:07:28.918 --> 00:07:31.452
There's no way out of here except through the house.

00:07:31.512 --> 00:07:32.673
Get behind the tree.

00:07:32.733 --> 00:07:33.584
What?

00:07:33.644 --> 00:07:35.065
Get behind the tree.

00:07:35.125 --> 00:07:37.879
Jack, are you out here?

00:07:37.938 --> 00:07:39.330
Jack?

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.722
Well, hi, Marie.

00:07:41.782 --> 00:07:43.898
You with someone, Jack.

00:07:43.958 --> 00:07:46.441
Will someone show as hell not?

00:07:46.501 --> 00:07:47.931
I'm just taking the air.

00:07:47.991 --> 00:07:49.161
There's someone here.

00:07:49.221 --> 00:07:50.662
I know there is.

00:07:50.722 --> 00:07:54.162
I think she's here.

00:07:54.182 --> 00:07:57.703
I like all my hair you bitch.

00:07:57.763 --> 00:07:59.834
You're calling me a bitch.

00:07:59.894 --> 00:08:01.134
Let go of me.

00:08:01.194 --> 00:08:06.925
You come after my husband on my wedding day and you call me a bitch.

00:08:06.945 --> 00:08:08.566
Let go of me.

00:08:08.606 --> 00:08:10.756
Give me one good reason why I should do that.

00:08:10.816 --> 00:08:11.386
Stop it.

00:08:11.446 --> 00:08:12.507
Let me go.

00:08:12.527 --> 00:08:13.167
Okay.

00:08:13.227 --> 00:08:14.107
I'll let go.

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:16.528
You're crazy.

00:08:16.588 --> 00:08:20.809
And now you're calling me names?

00:08:20.869 --> 00:08:23.420
Don't you dare call me names.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:26.191
Why you?

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.721
Get up.

00:08:28.781 --> 00:08:30.061
Don't get me again.

00:08:30.121 --> 00:08:31.992
Are you trying to kill me or something?

00:08:32.052 --> 00:08:35.653
I'm not gonna touch you again, you piece of garbage.

00:08:35.713 --> 00:08:41.364
But if you ever go near my husband again, I really will kill you.

00:08:41.425 --> 00:08:43.158
Now get out of here.

00:08:43.218 --> 00:08:45.912
You're a mad woman, Marie Loveau.

00:08:45.972 --> 00:08:48.024
You regret doing this.

00:08:48.084 --> 00:08:50.256
Marie, are you okay?

00:08:50.316 --> 00:08:51.266
I'm fine, Blanche.

00:08:51.286 --> 00:08:52.448
Do you need any help?

00:08:52.508 --> 00:08:53.388
No, go away.

00:08:53.408 --> 00:08:55.650
I want to talk to Jacques alone.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:58.492
Okay, but yell if you need me.

00:08:58.512 --> 00:08:59.993
Okay.

00:09:00.053 --> 00:09:01.433
Marie.

00:09:01.453 --> 00:09:02.764
Don't talk, Jack.

00:09:02.824 --> 00:09:04.434
Just listen.

00:09:04.494 --> 00:09:08.997
This is our wedding day, and I've just found you with another woman.

00:09:09.057 --> 00:09:11.808
Marie, we were just talking, in fact.

00:09:11.868 --> 00:09:12.939
I was just telling...

00:09:12.979 --> 00:09:13.819
I said, listen!

00:09:13.879 --> 00:09:19.432
You're my husband now, and from now on, you do things the way I want them.

00:09:19.492 --> 00:09:20.942
I was just...

00:09:20.982 --> 00:09:22.233
You hurt me, Jack.

00:09:22.293 --> 00:09:26.438
We are man and wife, and we do things my way.

00:09:26.498 --> 00:09:29.482
Are you serious?

00:09:29.542 --> 00:09:31.985
We're gonna do things your way?

00:09:32.045 --> 00:09:32.936
That's right.

00:09:32.996 --> 00:09:33.827
Uh-uh.

00:09:33.887 --> 00:09:36.680
No one tells me what to do, Marie.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.922
I'm a free man, remember?

00:09:38.982 --> 00:09:40.374
I ain't a slave.

00:09:40.434 --> 00:09:44.768
If you think you got yourself a slave when you married me, you're wrong.

00:09:44.828 --> 00:09:47.170
It doesn't make no difference that we're married.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:51.325
I'm gonna do things my way and no one is gonna stop me.

00:09:51.385 --> 00:09:54.197
You're gonna do things your way.

00:09:54.217 --> 00:09:56.008
I sure am.

00:09:56.068 --> 00:09:58.500
And that includes seeing other women.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.223
Marie, I will go where I want.

00:10:02.283 --> 00:10:07.006
See who I want and do what I want.

00:10:07.066 --> 00:10:11.510
And there ain't a damn thing you can do about it.

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:15.543
Oh, Jacques, you should not have said that.

00:10:15.603 --> 00:10:18.814
You really shouldn't have said that.

00:10:18.874 --> 00:10:25.896
You have to learn never, ever, to make me angry.

00:10:25.956 --> 00:10:29.916
Marie, are you okay?

00:10:29.976 --> 00:10:31.247
No, Blanche.

00:10:31.307 --> 00:10:32.718
I'm not okay.

00:10:32.778 --> 00:10:34.038
Where's Jack?

00:10:34.098 --> 00:10:36.729
I don't know, and I don't care.

00:10:36.789 --> 00:10:40.710
Marie, it's your wedding day.

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:47.002
You just got married, and you don't know where your husband is, and you don't care.

00:10:47.022 --> 00:10:48.293
No, Blanche.

00:10:48.353 --> 00:10:49.442
I don't.

00:10:49.502 --> 00:10:50.741
I agree.

00:10:50.801 --> 00:10:52.542
What's happened to you?

00:10:52.602 --> 00:10:53.962
What do you mean?

00:10:54.022 --> 00:10:56.424
You look different.

00:10:56.484 --> 00:10:57.995
Your eyes.

00:10:58.055 --> 00:11:00.906
I don't know what's happened to me, Blanche.

00:11:00.966 --> 00:11:03.798
But I sure as hell feel different.

00:11:03.858 --> 00:11:05.459
I feel...

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:07.070
angry and...

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:07.931
I don't know.

00:11:07.951 --> 00:11:10.348
I also feel strong.

00:11:10.408 --> 00:11:16.298
From now on, I'm not gonna take any nonsense from Jack or anyone.

00:11:16.358 --> 00:11:22.145
And first of all, I'm gonna take care of that little trap he was talking to.

00:11:22.205 --> 00:11:23.676
You know her name?

00:11:23.696 --> 00:11:25.589
I...

00:11:25.648 --> 00:11:28.682
No, I don't know her name.

00:11:28.742 --> 00:11:30.662
I think you do, Blanche.

00:11:30.722 --> 00:11:31.832
Tell me.

00:11:31.892 --> 00:11:32.782
Marie!

00:11:32.842 --> 00:11:33.953
Tell me!

00:11:34.013 --> 00:11:38.114
I think her name is Gina Baptiste.

00:11:38.174 --> 00:11:40.484
Do you know where she lives?

00:11:40.544 --> 00:11:41.044
No.

00:11:41.104 --> 00:11:42.435
Really, I don't.

00:11:42.495 --> 00:11:45.386
Branch, find out where she lives for me.

00:11:45.446 --> 00:11:49.596
Okay, but Branch, don't try to tell me what to do.

00:11:49.656 --> 00:11:51.437
It's too late for that.

00:11:51.497 --> 00:11:53.398
Okay, Marie.

00:11:53.458 --> 00:11:56.926
I'll find out where she lives.

00:11:56.986 --> 00:12:03.500
A few days later, Gina was in her room at the room in house.

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:05.892
Who's there?

00:12:05.952 --> 00:12:08.306
Is that you, Jack?

00:12:08.366 --> 00:12:10.178
Jack?

00:12:10.238 --> 00:12:11.549
Jack?

00:12:11.609 --> 00:12:13.441
Are you...

00:12:13.461 --> 00:12:16.690
What the hell is...

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:21.018
What's going on up there?

00:12:21.078 --> 00:12:23.399
This is disgusting.

00:12:23.459 --> 00:12:24.909
What's all the fuss about?

00:12:24.969 --> 00:12:27.419
Did you see anyone coming up to my door?

00:12:27.479 --> 00:12:30.540
Lady, there's always people coming to your door.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.660
Someone just knocked on my door.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.180
Did you see anyone?

00:12:34.221 --> 00:12:36.601
Well, I saw a woman going up the stairs.

00:12:36.661 --> 00:12:38.601
What did she look like?

00:12:38.661 --> 00:12:40.332
I didn't see her face.

00:12:40.392 --> 00:12:42.232
Anyway, what you yelling about?

00:12:42.292 --> 00:12:43.903
Look!

00:12:43.963 --> 00:12:46.274
My law, jeez!

00:12:46.334 --> 00:12:48.866
There's blood everywhere!

00:12:48.926 --> 00:12:49.966
What is it?

00:12:50.026 --> 00:12:50.847
What is it?

00:12:50.887 --> 00:12:53.538
Well, it was an animal.

00:12:53.598 --> 00:12:59.192
Chicken, I guess, now it's just blood and feathers and bones and stuff.

00:12:59.252 --> 00:13:00.953
And look at my door!

00:13:01.013 --> 00:13:03.354
There's blood on my door!

00:13:03.414 --> 00:13:04.525
Oh, my God!

00:13:04.585 --> 00:13:05.466
What is it?

00:13:05.526 --> 00:13:08.798
Someone wrote the letter M on your dog.

00:13:08.858 --> 00:13:10.018
What does it mean?

00:13:10.078 --> 00:13:10.839
Lady.

00:13:10.899 --> 00:13:13.340
You ain't from New Orleans, are you?

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:14.081
No.

00:13:14.141 --> 00:13:16.992
Why did they write M on my door?

00:13:17.052 --> 00:13:18.844
Don't you know nothing?

00:13:18.904 --> 00:13:21.845
It's the first letter of the word Mort.

00:13:21.905 --> 00:13:23.416
That's French.

00:13:23.476 --> 00:13:25.527
It means death.

00:13:25.587 --> 00:13:28.909
And it's written on your doll in blood.

00:13:28.969 --> 00:13:34.647
Man, someone just put a curse on you.

00:13:34.707 --> 00:13:41.316
Of course, it was Marie who wrote the letter M in blood on Gina's door.

00:13:41.377 --> 00:13:46.451
Afterwards, she went out into the street and ran in the direction of her house.

00:13:46.511 --> 00:13:50.782
But she didn't make it.

00:13:50.842 --> 00:13:54.363
I'm sorry.

00:13:54.424 --> 00:13:55.704
I didn't see you.

00:13:55.764 --> 00:13:58.355
Mom, just hold on there, Mom.

00:13:58.415 --> 00:13:59.305
I'm sorry.

00:13:59.365 --> 00:14:00.835
I didn't mean to run into you now.

00:14:00.875 --> 00:14:02.836
If you don't mind, I'll just be going.

00:14:02.896 --> 00:14:08.367
I said, hold on there and calm down.

00:14:08.427 --> 00:14:11.528
Now, are you okay?

00:14:11.588 --> 00:14:12.798
I'm fine.

00:14:12.858 --> 00:14:17.810
Mom, you have blood all over your hands and your clothes.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.068
Oh, my God.

00:14:19.128 --> 00:14:22.819
I think you should tell me what's going on here.

00:14:22.879 --> 00:14:23.510
No!

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:25.671
Take your hands off me and let me go!

00:14:25.731 --> 00:14:28.652
Mom, maybe you don't know me.

00:14:28.712 --> 00:14:30.744
But I can help you.

00:14:30.804 --> 00:14:32.615
What are you talking about?

00:14:32.675 --> 00:14:33.616
Who are you?

00:14:33.676 --> 00:14:36.818
My name is John Bayou.

00:14:36.878 --> 00:14:38.449
John Bayou?

00:14:38.509 --> 00:14:39.520
Yes.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:45.741
But around here, people called me Dr. John.

00:14:45.801 --> 00:14:47.760
Doctor John.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:51.253
Oh Lord Jesus, you're a voodoo doctor.

00:14:51.313 --> 00:14:56.237
Mom, I'm just a preacher in a church for freed slaves.

00:14:56.297 --> 00:15:00.731
I don't really like the expression voodoo doctor.

00:15:00.791 --> 00:15:02.322
But it's what you are.

00:15:02.382 --> 00:15:03.613
Leave me alone.

00:15:03.673 --> 00:15:05.294
I don't want to talk to you.

00:15:05.354 --> 00:15:08.056
Mom, you look like you're in big trouble.

00:15:08.116 --> 00:15:10.238
I don't want help from no voodoo doctor.

00:15:10.298 --> 00:15:12.890
Now, you listen to me.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.964
You need help.

00:15:15.024 --> 00:15:17.256
I can smell death on it.

00:15:17.316 --> 00:15:18.978
I ain't killed no one.

00:15:19.038 --> 00:15:22.530
Just calm down and just...

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:28.624
Right now I'm probably the only person in New Orleans who can help you.

00:15:28.684 --> 00:15:30.165
Now come with me.

00:15:30.225 --> 00:15:30.946
Where?

00:15:31.006 --> 00:15:32.427
Where are you taking me?

00:15:32.467 --> 00:15:34.858
Just across the street.

00:15:34.918 --> 00:15:37.060
Somewhere we can talk.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.302
across the street to that bar.

00:15:40.362 --> 00:15:41.413
That's right.

00:15:41.433 --> 00:15:43.254
I'm not going into a bar.

00:15:43.314 --> 00:15:45.245
I'm a respectable woman.

00:15:45.305 --> 00:15:48.037
A respectable married woman.

00:15:48.097 --> 00:15:55.342
I know you're a respectable woman, but you need to clean up and we need to talk.

00:15:55.402 --> 00:15:58.464
You can't go anywhere looking like that.

00:15:58.524 --> 00:16:00.534
Oh God.

00:16:00.594 --> 00:16:04.318
There are people across the street who can help you.

00:16:04.378 --> 00:16:11.053
Now let's go.

00:16:11.113 --> 00:16:18.679
Yes, she is, Doctor John.

00:16:18.699 --> 00:16:20.800
She's all cleaned up now.

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:22.021
Thank you, Celeste.

00:16:22.081 --> 00:16:23.802
Any time, Doctor.

00:16:23.862 --> 00:16:26.163
Anything else I can do for you?

00:16:26.223 --> 00:16:27.664
No, thank you, Celeste.

00:16:27.724 --> 00:16:29.745
You've been more than helpful.

00:16:29.765 --> 00:16:30.345
Okay.

00:16:30.405 --> 00:16:33.938
Well, you know where I am, if you need me.

00:16:33.998 --> 00:16:36.398
I don't like it here.

00:16:36.458 --> 00:16:38.019
People are looking at me.

00:16:38.079 --> 00:16:40.400
Only in your imagination.

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:43.814
They all got plenty of other things to think about.

00:16:43.874 --> 00:16:47.117
I want to say sorry.

00:16:47.177 --> 00:16:49.627
I wasn't very nice to you.

00:16:49.688 --> 00:16:51.718
You don't need to apologize.

00:16:51.778 --> 00:16:57.060
You just need to tell me what's going on.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.250
You could stop by telling me your name.

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:03.681
My name is Marie Paris.

00:17:03.741 --> 00:17:05.472
Marie Paris?

00:17:05.532 --> 00:17:09.002
I'm married to a man named Jack Paris.

00:17:09.062 --> 00:17:10.817
Maybe you've heard of him.

00:17:10.878 --> 00:17:15.901
Oh my goodness, yes, everyone in New Orleans knows Jack about us.

00:17:15.961 --> 00:17:19.568
I didn't realize he had such a fine looking wife.

00:17:19.628 --> 00:17:24.248
Well, we've only been married for a week or so, but my...

00:17:24.309 --> 00:17:28.665
Jackie is not an easy man to be married to.

00:17:28.725 --> 00:17:32.008
Well, I'm sure you're right about that.

00:17:32.068 --> 00:17:34.920
Mr. Bayou, this is not a laughing matter.

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.932
I've just done something terrible.

00:17:36.992 --> 00:17:37.782
Okay.

00:17:37.842 --> 00:17:42.316
If you want me to help, you have to tell me what happened.

00:17:42.376 --> 00:17:44.378
Okay.

00:17:44.438 --> 00:17:47.754
There was a woman at our wedding party.

00:17:47.814 --> 00:17:49.228
I didn't know her.

00:17:49.288 --> 00:17:50.829
I don't know how she got there.

00:17:50.889 --> 00:17:53.711
Anyway, she knew my husband and...

00:17:53.771 --> 00:17:55.282
Yes.

00:17:55.342 --> 00:18:01.196
I think my husband was planning to see her, like, secretly.

00:18:01.256 --> 00:18:02.708
I see.

00:18:02.768 --> 00:18:03.858
Go on.

00:18:03.918 --> 00:18:07.480
I went to the place where she lives and...

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.042
And?

00:18:09.102 --> 00:18:12.684
What did you do, Mary?

00:18:12.704 --> 00:18:16.277
I drew the letter M on her door, in blood.

00:18:16.337 --> 00:18:17.398
Ah.

00:18:17.458 --> 00:18:19.719
I just wanted to frighten her.

00:18:19.779 --> 00:18:21.100
Right.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.431
Well, I guess I can understand that.

00:18:23.491 --> 00:18:24.792
But there's something else.

00:18:24.852 --> 00:18:25.512
What?

00:18:25.572 --> 00:18:29.194
Well, I waited to see what happened.

00:18:29.254 --> 00:18:32.415
I sat on the stairs just above her room.

00:18:32.476 --> 00:18:36.798
While I was sitting there, I started to imagine things.

00:18:36.858 --> 00:18:38.638
I couldn't stop myself.

00:18:38.698 --> 00:18:40.650
What did you imagine, Marion?

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:45.128
I imagined that I was stabbing her like with a knife.

00:18:45.188 --> 00:18:48.036
Well, you only imagined that.

00:18:48.096 --> 00:18:49.106
I know.

00:18:49.166 --> 00:18:50.547
But she screamed.

00:18:50.607 --> 00:18:51.398
She did what?

00:18:51.458 --> 00:18:52.608
She screamed.

00:18:52.668 --> 00:18:54.459
I could hear her through the door.

00:18:54.519 --> 00:18:57.070
I imagined stabbing her with a knife.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:58.841
And I could hear her screaming.

00:18:58.901 --> 00:19:02.032
And then...

00:19:02.092 --> 00:19:07.845
I can't stop it anymore.

00:19:07.905 --> 00:19:10.876
I've got to get out of here.

00:19:10.936 --> 00:19:13.548
Hello, Gina.

00:19:13.608 --> 00:19:14.392
You.

00:19:14.452 --> 00:19:15.778
It's you.

00:19:15.838 --> 00:19:18.359
What are you doing to me?

00:19:18.419 --> 00:19:20.430
I ain't doing nothing, Gina.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:22.972
You're killing me.

00:19:23.032 --> 00:19:25.524
I ain't putting a finger on you, Gina.

00:19:25.584 --> 00:19:27.314
But you're gonna die.

00:19:27.374 --> 00:19:28.805
I'm certain of that.

00:19:28.865 --> 00:19:33.438
You're a bad woman and you deserve to die.

00:19:33.498 --> 00:19:35.429
Stop it!

00:19:35.489 --> 00:19:37.029
I left me out of here!

00:19:37.089 --> 00:19:38.890
You ain't going nowhere, you tramp!

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:39.310
Let me!

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:40.141
I don't know!

00:19:40.201 --> 00:19:41.241
You ain't leaving!

00:19:41.301 --> 00:19:43.892
I have to get out of here!

00:19:43.912 --> 00:19:44.582
The window!

00:19:44.642 --> 00:19:47.094
I can get out through the window!

00:19:47.154 --> 00:19:49.424
Someone help me!

00:19:49.484 --> 00:19:50.534
You okay, ma'am?

00:19:50.594 --> 00:19:51.665
I'm dying!

00:19:51.725 --> 00:19:53.516
I have to get out of here!

00:19:53.576 --> 00:19:55.676
Hey, ma'am, you'd be careful.

00:19:55.736 --> 00:19:57.047
You're gonna fall!

00:19:57.107 --> 00:20:00.042
Stop!

00:20:00.102 --> 00:20:04.448
Someone get a doctor!

00:20:04.508 --> 00:20:06.068
It's too late.

00:20:06.128 --> 00:20:10.970
There ain't nothing a doctor can do now.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:18.122
So she jumped from her balcony and now she's dead.

00:20:18.182 --> 00:20:20.113
Are you sure that's what happened?

00:20:20.173 --> 00:20:21.023
Yes.

00:20:21.083 --> 00:20:24.074
I came out of the room in-house and I saw her.

00:20:24.134 --> 00:20:26.435
Did anyone see you leave the room in-house?

00:20:26.495 --> 00:20:27.556
No.

00:20:27.616 --> 00:20:30.946
Everyone was looking at her lying dead in the street.

00:20:31.006 --> 00:20:32.305
Uh-huh.

00:20:32.365 --> 00:20:34.434
I'm not sorry she's dead.

00:20:34.494 --> 00:20:36.605
She was a bitch and a tramp.

00:20:36.665 --> 00:20:39.016
But I didn't kill her.

00:20:39.077 --> 00:20:45.980
I just feel that suddenly I have this power and I'm scared.

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:47.562
I don't want it.

00:20:47.622 --> 00:20:52.314
Well, Marie, this ain't something you can choose.

00:20:52.375 --> 00:20:55.336
You don't go looking for this kind of power.

00:20:55.396 --> 00:20:57.137
The power finds you.

00:20:57.197 --> 00:21:00.809
Listen, you don't understand what's happening to you right now.

00:21:00.869 --> 00:21:02.419
But I do.

00:21:02.479 --> 00:21:03.948
You need help.

00:21:04.008 --> 00:21:05.629
What kind of help?

00:21:05.689 --> 00:21:09.060
You need to come with me to Plaskongo.

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.681
Plaskongo?

00:21:10.741 --> 00:21:12.271
I ain't going there.

00:21:12.332 --> 00:21:13.552
It's too dangerous.

00:21:13.612 --> 00:21:16.863
They're crazy people doing crazy stuff there.

00:21:16.923 --> 00:21:19.794
Crazy dancing, beating on drums.

00:21:19.854 --> 00:21:21.515
I'm too scared to go there.

00:21:21.575 --> 00:21:26.877
Marie is just a place where people go to worship the God they believe in.

00:21:26.937 --> 00:21:28.158
I ain't going.

00:21:28.218 --> 00:21:29.597
Okay?

00:21:29.658 --> 00:21:35.733
But if you change your mind, meet me there on Sunday night.

00:21:35.793 --> 00:21:41.929
Soon after Marie arrived home, Jack walked through the door.

00:21:41.989 --> 00:21:44.041
Marie!

00:21:44.101 --> 00:21:45.453
Marie!

00:21:45.513 --> 00:21:46.214
Where are you?

00:21:46.274 --> 00:21:47.154
I'm here.

00:21:47.214 --> 00:21:48.586
In the pantry.

00:21:48.646 --> 00:21:49.788
What do you want?

00:21:49.848 --> 00:21:52.326
What the hell do you think you're doing?

00:21:52.386 --> 00:21:54.413
I'm not doing anything, Jack.

00:21:54.473 --> 00:21:57.144
I'm just sitting here minding my own business.

00:21:57.204 --> 00:22:02.166
Minding your own business is killing someone minding your own business.

00:22:02.226 --> 00:22:03.996
What are you talking about, Jack?

00:22:04.036 --> 00:22:05.807
You know what I'm talking about.

00:22:05.867 --> 00:22:06.798
Has someone died?

00:22:06.858 --> 00:22:09.348
You know damn well that someone has died.

00:22:09.408 --> 00:22:10.949
Gina is dead.

00:22:11.009 --> 00:22:12.220
Gina?

00:22:12.280 --> 00:22:16.121
Is that the woman I found you with at our wedding?

00:22:16.181 --> 00:22:18.301
You know who I'm talking about.

00:22:18.361 --> 00:22:19.611
How did she die?

00:22:19.671 --> 00:22:21.592
Stop playing games with me, Marie.

00:22:21.652 --> 00:22:23.553
I ain't playing games, Jack.

00:22:23.613 --> 00:22:25.384
Did she have an accident?

00:22:25.404 --> 00:22:26.525
No, Marie.

00:22:26.585 --> 00:22:29.046
She didn't have an accident.

00:22:29.106 --> 00:22:35.820
Folks who were in the street say that she came out on her balcony screaming fit to wake in the dead.

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:40.064
She was yelling that someone was stabbing her with a knife.

00:22:40.124 --> 00:22:42.786
Was someone stabbing her, Jack?

00:22:42.846 --> 00:22:44.150
No, Marie.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:46.112
No one was stabbing her.

00:22:46.172 --> 00:22:49.145
But she thought someone was stabbing her.

00:22:49.206 --> 00:22:50.176
And?

00:22:50.236 --> 00:22:53.390
And she threw herself off the balcony.

00:22:53.450 --> 00:22:55.572
She's dead, Marie.

00:22:55.632 --> 00:22:59.367
And you expect me to feel sad about that?

00:22:59.427 --> 00:23:00.468
Listen to me.

00:23:00.528 --> 00:23:01.640
No, Jacques.

00:23:01.700 --> 00:23:03.757
You listen to me.

00:23:03.817 --> 00:23:09.168
You wanted to go with that worthless tramp on our wedding day.

00:23:09.228 --> 00:23:11.499
On our wedding day, Jacques.

00:23:11.559 --> 00:23:15.593
The day that should have been the most important day of my life.

00:23:15.653 --> 00:23:17.534
And you ruined it all.

00:23:17.594 --> 00:23:20.227
You didn't have to kill her.

00:23:20.287 --> 00:23:21.188
Jacques.

00:23:21.248 --> 00:23:23.980
I didn't lay a finger on that whore.

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.741
I'm glad she's dead.

00:23:25.802 --> 00:23:27.203
It's what she deserves.

00:23:27.263 --> 00:23:29.335
But I did not touch her.

00:23:29.395 --> 00:23:31.035
You killed her.

00:23:31.095 --> 00:23:33.108
You did it somehow.

00:23:33.168 --> 00:23:34.572
I know you did.

00:23:34.632 --> 00:23:42.920
And I ain't staying in the same house as you any longer.

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:50.620
Well, Marie, nice to see you.

00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:52.691
Welcome to Plascongo.

00:23:52.751 --> 00:23:54.132
What's going on here?

00:23:54.192 --> 00:23:55.242
It's scary.

00:23:55.302 --> 00:23:59.704
It's just people having a good time, Marie.

00:23:59.764 --> 00:24:02.496
There ain't nothing to worry about.

00:24:02.556 --> 00:24:04.557
Hey, lady, come on, Blance.

00:24:04.617 --> 00:24:07.398
You tell her, Matt, he'll take your hands off me.

00:24:07.458 --> 00:24:08.959
Oh, come now, lady.

00:24:09.019 --> 00:24:10.280
I ain't gonna hurt you.

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:13.384
You heard what the lady said, sir.

00:24:13.444 --> 00:24:14.608
Oh yeah?

00:24:14.668 --> 00:24:16.700
And who the hell do you think you are?

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:18.622
Hey, lay off Matthew.

00:24:18.682 --> 00:24:20.713
That's John Byou.

00:24:20.773 --> 00:24:22.294
John Byou.

00:24:22.354 --> 00:24:23.835
Oh my God.

00:24:23.895 --> 00:24:25.186
Dr. John.

00:24:25.246 --> 00:24:26.076
Sorry.

00:24:26.136 --> 00:24:27.208
Mr. Byou.

00:24:27.268 --> 00:24:31.190
I think you better say sorry to the lady as well, so.

00:24:31.250 --> 00:24:32.772
Sorry, Lady.

00:24:32.832 --> 00:24:34.222
Sorry I spoke to you.

00:24:34.282 --> 00:24:35.564
Come on!

00:24:35.624 --> 00:24:40.276
Well, John, you certainly have the power, too.

00:24:40.336 --> 00:24:41.488
Maybe.

00:24:41.548 --> 00:24:42.698
Anyway.

00:24:42.758 --> 00:24:45.030
You don't need to feel afraid.

00:24:45.090 --> 00:24:47.172
I don't feel afraid when I'm with you.

00:24:47.192 --> 00:24:49.864
But what's going on here?

00:24:49.924 --> 00:24:56.542
Well, most people here are just here to talk, dance, be with their friends.

00:24:56.602 --> 00:25:00.246
But there's some religious stuff going on too.

00:25:00.306 --> 00:25:01.368
John!

00:25:01.428 --> 00:25:02.519
What is it?

00:25:02.579 --> 00:25:04.000
That man over there.

00:25:04.060 --> 00:25:05.572
The one near the fire.

00:25:05.632 --> 00:25:06.752
What about him?

00:25:06.812 --> 00:25:10.416
He's dancing and he's holding a snake.

00:25:10.476 --> 00:25:12.858
The snake is wrapped around his body.

00:25:12.878 --> 00:25:14.329
That's right.

00:25:14.389 --> 00:25:15.730
What's he doing?

00:25:15.790 --> 00:25:17.342
Don't worry, Marie.

00:25:17.402 --> 00:25:19.424
He's a voodoo preacher.

00:25:19.484 --> 00:25:23.247
Snicks are very special creatures to voodoo people.

00:25:23.307 --> 00:25:24.948
But what's happening?

00:25:25.009 --> 00:25:27.606
The voodoo service is started.

00:25:27.666 --> 00:25:29.463
And he afraid of the snake?

00:25:29.523 --> 00:25:32.114
No, Marie, he ain't afraid of the snake.

00:25:32.174 --> 00:25:34.914
And you mustn't be afraid either.

00:25:34.974 --> 00:25:38.266
What do you mean, I mustn't be afraid?

00:25:38.326 --> 00:25:42.758
Marie, he may choose to give the snake to someone.

00:25:42.818 --> 00:25:45.098
It's part of the service.

00:25:45.158 --> 00:25:48.650
He may choose to give the snake to you.

00:25:48.710 --> 00:25:50.390
Give me the snake.

00:25:50.450 --> 00:25:51.310
Why?

00:25:51.370 --> 00:25:55.348
Don't be afraid if he asks you to take the snake.

00:25:55.408 --> 00:25:56.776
Are you crazy?

00:25:56.836 --> 00:25:58.096
No way.

00:25:58.156 --> 00:26:00.808
I'm not going anywhere near Snake.

00:26:00.868 --> 00:26:02.640
Snake scare me to death.

00:26:02.700 --> 00:26:06.902
Marie, you have nothing to fear from the Snake.

00:26:06.962 --> 00:26:09.784
You have the power to control you.

00:26:09.844 --> 00:26:12.226
John, I can't do it.

00:26:12.286 --> 00:26:19.792
I can't stay here.

00:26:19.852 --> 00:26:28.690
Marie, there ain't no place you can go.

00:26:28.750 --> 00:26:32.434
If the preacher wants to find you, he'll find you.

00:26:32.494 --> 00:26:34.316
Why are you saying this?

00:26:34.376 --> 00:26:36.798
You said I should come here to get help.

00:26:36.858 --> 00:26:39.190
Then you'll scare me nearly to death.

00:26:39.250 --> 00:26:41.252
Marie, trust me.

00:26:41.312 --> 00:26:42.042
Why?

00:26:42.102 --> 00:26:53.236
Why should I trust you?

00:26:53.296 --> 00:27:04.238
God's sake!

00:27:04.298 --> 00:27:05.668
What's he saying?

00:27:05.728 --> 00:27:08.499
He's speaking to Dambalawido.

00:27:08.559 --> 00:27:11.580
Dambalawido is the voodoo snake.

00:27:11.640 --> 00:27:12.560
Go.

00:27:12.620 --> 00:27:15.221
Dambalawido.

00:27:15.281 --> 00:27:18.162
Give me a sign.

00:27:18.222 --> 00:27:20.842
Give me a sign.

00:27:20.902 --> 00:27:28.375
How about me?

00:27:28.435 --> 00:27:36.308
He is coming towards you, Mary.

00:27:36.368 --> 00:27:38.678
John, help me!

00:27:38.738 --> 00:27:40.439
You!

00:27:40.499 --> 00:27:43.980
Lady will be long black here.

00:27:44.040 --> 00:27:45.740
What do you want?

00:27:45.800 --> 00:27:48.191
Take this name.

00:27:48.251 --> 00:27:49.482
No!

00:27:49.542 --> 00:27:52.332
Take this name!

00:27:52.392 --> 00:27:57.196
Take this name!

00:27:57.257 --> 00:28:01.942
Oh my god!

00:28:02.002 --> 00:28:03.933
Fear the power, Marie!

00:28:03.993 --> 00:28:05.714
You have the power!

00:28:05.774 --> 00:28:08.326
And the power will save you!

