00:41:18.172 --> 00:41:20.192
A piece of clothing?

00:41:20.252 --> 00:41:22.073
You mean like a shirt?

00:41:22.133 --> 00:41:22.913
Yes.

00:41:22.973 --> 00:41:24.634
Something like that.

00:41:24.694 --> 00:41:26.044
Don't worry.

00:41:26.104 --> 00:41:27.874
Your son won't hang.

00:41:27.935 --> 00:41:29.756
I'll make sure of that.

00:41:29.816 --> 00:41:32.279
Oh, thank you, Mrs. Loveville.

00:41:32.339 --> 00:41:36.000
Thank you.

00:41:36.060 --> 00:41:41.662
Marie did everything she could to help people.

00:41:41.722 --> 00:41:45.693
And of course, when she was successful, people paid her.

00:41:45.753 --> 00:41:48.304
In fact, she made a lot of money.

00:41:48.364 --> 00:41:52.645
So much money that she moved into a new house on Bourbon Street.

00:41:52.706 --> 00:41:57.802
Her only companion there was a black cat named Bayou.

00:41:57.862 --> 00:41:59.748
By you.

00:41:59.808 --> 00:42:01.158
Come here.

00:42:01.218 --> 00:42:04.922
I got you something real tasty.

00:42:04.982 --> 00:42:12.278
Then one day she had a visitor who was looking for something a little more personal.

00:42:12.338 --> 00:42:15.200
Well, by you.

00:42:15.260 --> 00:42:17.102
Who can that be?

00:42:17.162 --> 00:42:18.764
Hold on.

00:42:18.824 --> 00:42:20.335
I'm coming.

00:42:20.395 --> 00:42:23.027
Well, well, well.

00:42:23.088 --> 00:42:25.253
Guess who's here?

00:42:25.313 --> 00:42:31.749
It was Jack Paris, the no good low life who also happened to be Marie's husband.

00:42:31.809 --> 00:42:35.080
Jack, what the hell do you want?

00:42:35.140 --> 00:42:39.261
Now come on Marie, is that any way to welcome back y'all?

00:42:39.321 --> 00:42:40.882
Loving husband.

00:42:40.942 --> 00:42:42.802
Teach your hands off me.

00:42:42.862 --> 00:42:47.384
Oh come on Marie, this is no way for a wife to behave.

00:42:47.444 --> 00:42:51.277
Go away Jack, now and don't come back.

00:42:51.337 --> 00:42:54.601
I'll leave just as soon as I said what I came to say.

00:42:54.661 --> 00:42:56.422
And what's that?

00:42:56.482 --> 00:42:58.974
Well, do you mind if I come inside?

00:42:59.034 --> 00:43:03.787
If you have something to tell me, you can tell me right here at the door.

00:43:03.847 --> 00:43:06.809
Now you listen to me, Marie.

00:43:06.869 --> 00:43:14.820
You have five minutes to tell me what you want, and then I'm gonna call someone to throw you out.

00:43:14.880 --> 00:43:16.418
What?

00:43:16.478 --> 00:43:18.589
You gonna call the sheriff?

00:43:18.649 --> 00:43:21.010
I'm sure he'll be very happy to help.

00:43:21.070 --> 00:43:22.882
I don't need the sheriff.

00:43:22.942 --> 00:43:26.794
I have friends who could turn you in the dog meat if I ask them to.

00:43:26.854 --> 00:43:28.605
Don't threaten me, Marie.

00:43:28.665 --> 00:43:31.646
I threaten you all I want, Jack.

00:43:31.706 --> 00:43:34.988
Now, what do you want?

00:43:35.048 --> 00:43:36.120
Okay.

00:43:36.180 --> 00:43:40.400
Well, in case you forgot, we got married a few months back.

00:43:40.460 --> 00:43:41.668
Oh, that's right.

00:43:41.728 --> 00:43:42.748
We did.

00:43:42.808 --> 00:43:48.613
And in case you forgot, you hardly spent a week in my house before you disappeared.

00:43:48.673 --> 00:43:49.824
Yeah, well, that's right.

00:43:49.884 --> 00:43:54.146
But I don't even think about spending another night under my roof.

00:43:54.206 --> 00:43:55.968
Now, hold on there, Marie.

00:43:56.028 --> 00:44:01.510
At the time, I thought that somehow you were responsible for the death of...

00:44:01.571 --> 00:44:02.901
A friend of mine.

00:44:02.961 --> 00:44:06.984
If you're talking about that hard Gina Batiste, you better say.

00:44:07.044 --> 00:44:08.875
It's okay, Marie.

00:44:08.935 --> 00:44:11.517
I now know I was wrong.

00:44:11.577 --> 00:44:17.782
Gina's death was an accident, so I've come back to apologize for what I said.

00:44:17.842 --> 00:44:21.754
And I thought maybe we could start over.

00:44:21.814 --> 00:44:24.767
Turn over and no leave, you know.

00:44:24.827 --> 00:44:26.798
Wipe the slate clean.

00:44:26.859 --> 00:44:27.982
Huh?

00:44:28.042 --> 00:44:31.176
Wipe the slate clean.

00:44:31.236 --> 00:44:36.668
The only reason I would wipe a slate clean would be to break it over your head.

00:44:36.728 --> 00:44:38.118
Aw, come now, Marie!

00:44:38.138 --> 00:44:38.798
Jack!

00:44:38.858 --> 00:44:42.499
Marion, you was the biggest mistake I ever made.

00:44:42.559 --> 00:44:48.370
When you leave this house in about one minute from now, you ain't coming back.

00:44:48.430 --> 00:44:51.891
Well, don't be too sure of that, Marie.

00:44:51.951 --> 00:44:55.151
Don't forget that you and me are still man and wife.

00:44:55.211 --> 00:44:57.111
That's nonsense and you know it.

00:44:57.171 --> 00:44:58.792
It ain't nonsense, Marie.

00:44:58.852 --> 00:45:00.264
We're man and wife.

00:45:00.324 --> 00:45:03.786
So watch yours is also mine.

00:45:03.846 --> 00:45:05.076
What?

00:45:05.136 --> 00:45:07.098
We're married, Marie.

00:45:07.158 --> 00:45:10.330
And that means till death us do part.

00:45:10.390 --> 00:45:12.012
Watch yours is mine.

00:45:12.072 --> 00:45:13.913
Well, half mine.

00:45:13.973 --> 00:45:16.905
I own half of all of this.

00:45:16.965 --> 00:45:18.726
Are you crazy?

00:45:18.786 --> 00:45:24.092
And you have a mighty fine place here, Marie.

00:45:24.152 --> 00:45:26.424
Get out of here, Jack.

00:45:26.484 --> 00:45:32.699
I don't owe you anything, and you are not gonna get a silver dime out of me.

00:45:32.759 --> 00:45:35.451
Well, Marie, you may have forgotten.

00:45:35.511 --> 00:45:39.744
But in this city, there are laws about this kind of thing.

00:45:39.804 --> 00:45:44.598
I guess I'll just take my claim to court and see what they say.

00:45:44.658 --> 00:45:47.510
You can do what the hell you like.

00:45:47.570 --> 00:45:50.101
I ain't giving you a scent.

00:45:50.162 --> 00:45:54.622
Ah, now this may be someone who can help you change your mind.

00:45:54.682 --> 00:45:56.093
What did you say?

00:45:56.153 --> 00:45:58.594
There's someone who wants to talk to you.

00:45:58.654 --> 00:46:01.114
Open the door.

00:46:01.174 --> 00:46:03.105
Good morning.

00:46:03.165 --> 00:46:04.605
Can I help you?

00:46:04.666 --> 00:46:06.816
You must be Mrs. Paris.

00:46:06.876 --> 00:46:09.387
My name is Marie LaVoe.

00:46:09.447 --> 00:46:10.447
Who are you?

00:46:10.507 --> 00:46:13.368
My name is George Andrews.

00:46:13.428 --> 00:46:16.628
How can I help you, Mr. Andrews?

00:46:16.688 --> 00:46:20.279
Well, I think my client, Mr. Paris, is here.

00:46:20.339 --> 00:46:21.509
You're what?

00:46:21.569 --> 00:46:22.790
My client.

00:46:22.850 --> 00:46:24.370
I'm an attorney at law.

00:46:24.430 --> 00:46:28.511
I'm advising Mr. Paris on his claim to have for your estate.

00:46:28.571 --> 00:46:29.441
Why?

00:46:29.501 --> 00:46:32.772
You son of a bitch!

00:46:32.832 --> 00:46:36.972
Get out!

00:46:37.032 --> 00:46:38.483
Get out!

00:46:38.543 --> 00:46:40.190
Both of you!

00:46:40.250 --> 00:46:43.618
Mrs. Parris, you're making a big mistake here.

00:46:43.678 --> 00:46:46.050
Don't you call me Mrs. Parris.

00:46:46.110 --> 00:46:48.441
My name is Marie Lavaux.

00:46:48.501 --> 00:46:50.282
Now, get out!

00:46:50.342 --> 00:46:58.006
Mrs. Parris, since the day of your marriage to Mr. Parris, he has been legally entitled to one half for your estate.

00:46:58.066 --> 00:46:59.077
In view of Mrs. Parris.

00:46:59.097 --> 00:47:00.517
Did you hear me?

00:47:00.577 --> 00:47:01.458
Get out!

00:47:01.518 --> 00:47:04.069
Mrs. Parris!

00:47:04.129 --> 00:47:06.710
I told you.

00:47:06.770 --> 00:47:09.450
Don't call me Mrs. Parris.

00:47:09.510 --> 00:47:11.869
Jack, that's it.

00:47:11.929 --> 00:47:17.351
I want you to leave now and take your fat friend with you.

00:47:17.411 --> 00:47:20.863
You can't get rid of the problem by throwing us out, Marie.

00:47:20.923 --> 00:47:22.554
You want to bet money on that?

00:47:22.614 --> 00:47:24.935
You can bet your life on it.

00:47:24.995 --> 00:47:29.987
Mrs. Paris, I will instruct my client to press charges against you.

00:47:30.027 --> 00:47:33.239
Keep talking if you want me to hit you again.

00:47:33.299 --> 00:47:33.949
Fine.

00:47:34.009 --> 00:47:35.570
Okay, just hold on there.

00:47:35.630 --> 00:47:36.840
Goodbye, gentlemen.

00:47:36.900 --> 00:47:39.233
Have a nice day.

00:47:39.293 --> 00:47:44.027
Marie, you better think again about what you're doing.

00:47:44.087 --> 00:47:47.458
The next time we meet, we'll be in cult.

00:47:47.518 --> 00:47:52.802
The next time we meet, Jack Paris, we'll be in hell.

00:47:52.862 --> 00:48:00.556
Marie noticed that Jack had left his hat, and she thought about opening the door and throwing it out onto the street.

00:48:00.616 --> 00:48:02.976
But she didn't.

00:48:03.036 --> 00:48:05.938
Well, by you.

00:48:05.998 --> 00:48:10.021
What do you think we should do with Jack?

00:48:10.081 --> 00:48:15.254
Because he's gonna have to die.

00:48:15.314 --> 00:48:19.316
And die very soon.

00:48:19.376 --> 00:48:25.559
She took a sharp knife and began to cut the hat into small pieces.

00:48:25.619 --> 00:48:31.662
Then she put the pieces into a bowl of water.

00:48:31.722 --> 00:48:38.156
There's a lake near New Orleans called Lake Pontchartrain.

00:48:38.216 --> 00:48:46.728
A few days later, early in the morning before it was light, two fishermen were out on the lake in a boat.

00:48:46.788 --> 00:48:48.555
Hey!

00:48:48.615 --> 00:48:50.466
Help me with this nap!

00:48:50.526 --> 00:48:51.916
Well, what's the problem?

00:48:51.976 --> 00:48:53.317
I don't know!

00:48:53.377 --> 00:48:56.078
We got something real heavy in it!

00:48:56.138 --> 00:48:57.999
He wasn't matter with you!

00:48:58.059 --> 00:48:59.439
You losing your strength?

00:48:59.499 --> 00:49:01.950
You can't pull in the net without me helping you?

00:49:01.970 --> 00:49:04.751
Stop yelling and helping me with this nap!

00:49:04.811 --> 00:49:05.862
Let's do heavy!

00:49:05.922 --> 00:49:07.262
Hey, come on!

00:49:07.322 --> 00:49:10.463
Why can't it be so heavy that you can't hold it in?

00:49:10.523 --> 00:49:12.744
Just shut up and help me!

00:49:12.804 --> 00:49:17.352
Okay, let's do it!

00:49:17.412 --> 00:49:22.902
Hey, what the hell did we catch today?

00:49:22.962 --> 00:49:26.393
Oh, well you shut up and keep pulling.

00:49:26.453 --> 00:49:30.976
Okay, here it comes.

00:49:31.036 --> 00:49:32.686
Stop it.

00:49:32.746 --> 00:49:34.268
What's the matter?

00:49:34.328 --> 00:49:37.439
Look, in the net, is that?

00:49:37.499 --> 00:49:39.960
Is that someone's arm?

00:49:40.020 --> 00:49:41.741
Oh my God.

00:49:41.801 --> 00:49:44.122
Jesus, marry Joseph, it's a man.

00:49:44.142 --> 00:49:47.398
Come on, help me get him in the boat.

00:49:47.458 --> 00:49:48.793
In the boat?

00:49:48.853 --> 00:49:49.714
No way!

00:49:49.754 --> 00:49:51.305
But what you talking about?

00:49:51.365 --> 00:49:53.728
We have to take him back to the show.

00:49:53.788 --> 00:49:57.441
I ain't going nowhere with a dead body in the boat.

00:49:57.481 --> 00:49:58.652
No more, boy.

00:49:58.712 --> 00:50:00.053
What you thinking about?

00:50:00.113 --> 00:50:02.235
We can't leave his body here in the lake.

00:50:02.295 --> 00:50:03.576
We sure can.

00:50:03.636 --> 00:50:07.600
For pity's sake.

00:50:07.660 --> 00:50:08.350
What is it?

00:50:08.410 --> 00:50:10.342
I just saw his face.

00:50:10.402 --> 00:50:13.444
His eyes are staring at me.

00:50:13.504 --> 00:50:15.644
pushing back in the water.

00:50:15.704 --> 00:50:17.446
Let someone else find him.

00:50:17.506 --> 00:50:18.946
Okay.

00:50:19.006 --> 00:50:21.388
Jesus, man.

00:50:21.448 --> 00:50:23.500
That was terrible.

00:50:23.560 --> 00:50:28.224
His eyes were staring at me and his mouth was wide open.

00:50:28.284 --> 00:50:32.046
He looked like he was in fear of the devil when he died.

00:50:32.106 --> 00:50:33.347
Stop talking about it.

00:50:33.407 --> 00:50:34.378
I don't want to know.

00:50:34.438 --> 00:50:35.859
Let's get out of here.

00:50:35.919 --> 00:50:39.902
The worst thing is I recognized him.

00:50:39.962 --> 00:50:41.460
You did?

00:50:41.520 --> 00:50:43.789
Yeah, who was it?

00:50:43.849 --> 00:50:49.494
His name is Jack Paris.

00:50:49.554 --> 00:50:56.659
The next day, he revisited one of her hairdresser clients, a woman called Margaret Salinger.

00:50:56.720 --> 00:51:02.474
She lived in a fancy house in Dauphin Street, and her husband was a businessman.

00:51:02.534 --> 00:51:05.258
They seemed to have a lot of money.

00:51:05.318 --> 00:51:10.182
Mrs. Salinger lied gossiping with Marie.

00:51:10.243 --> 00:51:13.786
You know something, Marie.

00:51:13.846 --> 00:51:15.226
What's that, Margaret?

00:51:15.286 --> 00:51:18.788
You have a talent that no one else in the world has.

00:51:18.848 --> 00:51:19.819
I do.

00:51:19.879 --> 00:51:21.570
And what talent is that?

00:51:21.630 --> 00:51:26.052
You're the only person in this city who can make my hair look good.

00:51:26.112 --> 00:51:27.582
Oh, come on.

00:51:27.643 --> 00:51:29.243
I'm nothing special.

00:51:29.303 --> 00:51:30.884
Not true.

00:51:30.944 --> 00:51:35.156
I do believe that without you, I would look like a witch.

00:51:35.216 --> 00:51:36.657
Margaret, stop it.

00:51:36.717 --> 00:51:38.568
You're a fine-looking woman.

00:51:38.628 --> 00:51:40.926
Well, I don't know about that.

00:51:40.986 --> 00:51:43.905
But have you seen my daughter Laverne recently?

00:51:43.965 --> 00:51:48.849
She just turned 19 and she's a real good-looking girl.

00:51:48.909 --> 00:51:50.920
I have, and you're right.

00:51:50.980 --> 00:51:53.212
She's a real beauty.

00:51:53.272 --> 00:51:55.694
Margaret, I want to...

00:51:55.754 --> 00:51:56.915
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:51:56.975 --> 00:51:59.067
I didn't realize there was someone with you.

00:51:59.127 --> 00:52:00.728
What do you want, Henry?

00:52:00.788 --> 00:52:04.732
Margaret, I need to speak to you privately for a moment.

00:52:04.792 --> 00:52:06.633
Marie is doing my hair.

00:52:06.693 --> 00:52:07.764
Can't I wait?

00:52:07.784 --> 00:52:09.436
No, I'm afraid it can't.

00:52:09.496 --> 00:52:13.860
Is it something so secret that my hairdresser can't hear it?

00:52:13.920 --> 00:52:14.500
Well...

00:52:14.560 --> 00:52:17.652
Whatever it is, I'm sure I won't understand it.

00:52:17.712 --> 00:52:20.744
And I'm sure I'll forget it the minute I hear it.

00:52:20.804 --> 00:52:25.796
Yes, but if you don't mind, I need to talk to my wife alone.

00:52:25.856 --> 00:52:27.757
Oh, well, Marie.

00:52:27.817 --> 00:52:29.848
I guess I better listen to him.

00:52:29.908 --> 00:52:32.419
Perhaps you would like some lemon tea.

00:52:32.479 --> 00:52:34.640
Okay, I'll come back later.

00:52:34.700 --> 00:52:36.351
Go down to the kitchen, Marie.

00:52:36.411 --> 00:52:41.839
Betsy will look after you.

00:52:41.899 --> 00:52:47.637
Marie, how you doing?

00:52:47.697 --> 00:52:48.677
Fine, Betsy.

00:52:48.697 --> 00:52:49.937
You want some ice tea?

00:52:49.957 --> 00:52:50.958
That would be fine.

00:52:51.018 --> 00:52:54.849
Marie, I was so sorry to hear about Jack.

00:52:54.909 --> 00:52:59.880
Yes, well, you know, we weren't living together anymore.

00:52:59.940 --> 00:53:02.811
Well, yeah, I did hear that.

00:53:02.871 --> 00:53:05.862
But did they ever find out what happened to him?

00:53:05.922 --> 00:53:12.679
Well, I just think he got drunk as a skunk and fell in the lake.

00:53:12.739 --> 00:53:17.425
Marie, that's a terrible thing to say.

00:53:17.485 --> 00:53:19.596
Betsy, can I?

00:53:19.656 --> 00:53:21.056
Oh, sorry.

00:53:21.116 --> 00:53:22.556
Oh, hi, Laverne.

00:53:22.616 --> 00:53:24.607
Laverne, you know Marie, don't you?

00:53:24.667 --> 00:53:25.657
Yes, indeed.

00:53:25.677 --> 00:53:27.207
Hello, Mrs. Paris.

00:53:27.267 --> 00:53:28.418
Laverne.

00:53:28.478 --> 00:53:30.738
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:53:30.798 --> 00:53:32.029
Call me Marie.

00:53:32.089 --> 00:53:33.969
Right, okay.

00:53:34.029 --> 00:53:37.510
Marie, I'm sorry to hear about your husband.

00:53:37.570 --> 00:53:38.850
Thank you, Laverne.

00:53:38.910 --> 00:53:41.554
It must be so hard to lose someone you love.

00:53:41.614 --> 00:53:44.628
Yes, I guess it is.

00:53:44.688 --> 00:53:46.119
Young Laverne is in love.

00:53:46.179 --> 00:53:47.060
Ain't you Laverne?

00:53:47.120 --> 00:53:48.641
No, Betsey, stop it.

00:53:48.701 --> 00:53:51.392
Are you in love, Laverne?

00:53:51.432 --> 00:53:52.743
Yes, I am.

00:53:52.803 --> 00:53:53.914
Who's the lucky boy?

00:53:53.934 --> 00:53:59.737
His name is Tom Martin, and he works on one of the boats that sail to the islands.

00:53:59.797 --> 00:54:01.607
You know, the sugar boats?

00:54:01.667 --> 00:54:03.338
He works on a boat.

00:54:03.398 --> 00:54:04.308
Yes.

00:54:04.368 --> 00:54:09.169
I know it doesn't sound like much of a job, but he loves the sea.

00:54:09.229 --> 00:54:12.410
He wants to be captain of his own ship one day.

00:54:12.470 --> 00:54:14.950
I guess that means he's way a lot.

00:54:15.010 --> 00:54:16.331
Yes, he is.

00:54:16.391 --> 00:54:18.271
But he's coming home soon.

00:54:18.331 --> 00:54:19.791
That's great, Laverne.

00:54:19.851 --> 00:54:22.882
I hope you have a fine time when he comes back.

00:54:22.942 --> 00:54:24.742
I sure will, if...

00:54:24.803 --> 00:54:26.783
If what, Laverne?

00:54:26.843 --> 00:54:28.564
Nothing.

00:54:28.624 --> 00:54:41.804
Well, the thing is, Dad wants me to marry someone who's gonna make a lot of money, and Tom sure isn't gonna do that.

00:54:41.864 --> 00:54:52.678
So Henry, what is it that's so important it can't wait till I've had my air done?

00:54:52.738 --> 00:54:56.688
Margaret, there's something I have to tell you.

00:54:56.748 --> 00:54:58.259
What?

00:54:58.319 --> 00:55:00.861
What is it, Henry?

00:55:00.921 --> 00:55:04.514
Margaret, we are in deep trouble.

00:55:04.574 --> 00:55:05.615
Why?

00:55:05.675 --> 00:55:06.586
What's happened?

00:55:06.606 --> 00:55:07.947
I...

00:55:08.008 --> 00:55:10.300
I have lost a lot of money.

00:55:10.360 --> 00:55:11.510
How much?

00:55:11.571 --> 00:55:12.542
A lot.

00:55:12.602 --> 00:55:14.564
How much?

00:55:14.624 --> 00:55:16.888
Ten thousand dollars.

00:55:16.948 --> 00:55:17.788
Ten...

00:55:17.848 --> 00:55:21.424
You lost ten thousand dollars?

00:55:21.484 --> 00:55:24.819
I didn't know you had ten thousand dollars.

00:55:24.879 --> 00:55:25.800
I didn't.

00:55:25.860 --> 00:55:28.935
I borrowed the money and then I lost every cent.

00:55:28.995 --> 00:55:30.358
But how?

00:55:30.418 --> 00:55:32.881
I went into a land deal with a man.

00:55:32.901 --> 00:55:36.255
A terrible man called George Andrews.

00:55:36.316 --> 00:55:38.288
The man who was here this afternoon.

00:55:38.348 --> 00:55:41.042
That ugly little fat guy?

00:55:41.102 --> 00:55:41.853
Yes.

00:55:41.914 --> 00:55:43.246
He's a lawyer.

00:55:43.306 --> 00:55:44.757
And he's a crook.

00:55:44.817 --> 00:55:47.007
He stole all the money.

00:55:47.068 --> 00:55:50.117
Okay, so he committed a crime.

00:55:50.177 --> 00:55:51.588
Go tell a sheriff.

00:55:51.648 --> 00:55:52.898
I can't do that.

00:55:52.958 --> 00:55:56.100
The deal wasn't completely legal.

00:55:56.160 --> 00:55:57.862
I didn't realize it at the time.

00:55:57.882 --> 00:56:02.034
I guess I didn't read the small print in the contract.

00:56:02.094 --> 00:56:04.956
Henry, what are we going to do?

00:56:05.016 --> 00:56:08.628
This house isn't even worth $10,000.

00:56:08.688 --> 00:56:11.690
There is a solution.

00:56:11.750 --> 00:56:12.893
What's that?

00:56:12.953 --> 00:56:17.517
Andrews will pay me the money back and pay off all my other debts.

00:56:17.577 --> 00:56:19.618
And why would he do that?

00:56:19.678 --> 00:56:24.551
Well, first of all, he has agreed to buy the land we own out west of the city.

00:56:24.611 --> 00:56:28.553
That piece of land near the Achavelaya Swamp?

00:56:28.613 --> 00:56:29.594
Yes.

00:56:29.654 --> 00:56:34.996
He wants to buy that land for $10,000?

00:56:35.056 --> 00:56:36.557
That's great!

00:56:36.617 --> 00:56:38.088
Not exactly.

00:56:38.148 --> 00:56:40.420
There's something else that he wants.

00:56:40.480 --> 00:56:41.562
What?

00:56:41.622 --> 00:56:46.407
Well, Henry, what is it that he wants?

00:56:46.467 --> 00:56:49.448
This afternoon, he met Laverne.

00:56:49.508 --> 00:56:50.378
And?

00:56:50.438 --> 00:56:55.933
He, well, he has asked me for her hand in marriage.

00:56:55.993 --> 00:56:57.516
What?

00:56:57.576 --> 00:57:00.528
Henry, Laverne is 19.

00:57:00.588 --> 00:57:02.469
Well, yes.

00:57:02.489 --> 00:57:05.260
And he is old and fat and disgusting.

00:57:05.320 --> 00:57:11.713
Henry, I am not going to allow that horrible man to marry my daughter.

00:57:11.773 --> 00:57:14.984
Margaret, things aren't as simple as that.

00:57:15.044 --> 00:57:16.125
I'll explain.

00:57:16.185 --> 00:57:20.838
The thing is...

00:57:20.898 --> 00:57:25.476
Can I come in?

00:57:25.536 --> 00:57:26.984
Yes.

00:57:27.044 --> 00:57:28.555
Margaret.

00:57:28.615 --> 00:57:30.056
What's the matter?

00:57:30.116 --> 00:57:32.487
I just heard some terrible news.

00:57:32.548 --> 00:57:33.338
What?

00:57:33.398 --> 00:57:34.569
What's happened?

00:57:34.629 --> 00:57:37.781
Henry just told me that someone wants to marry Laverne.

00:57:37.841 --> 00:57:40.533
You mean the young man who works on the sugar boat?

00:57:40.593 --> 00:57:41.534
No, Marie.

00:57:41.594 --> 00:57:42.995
Not Tom.

00:57:43.055 --> 00:57:47.028
A horrible old man called George Andrews.

00:57:47.088 --> 00:57:49.540
George Andrews?

00:57:49.600 --> 00:57:50.966
Yes.

00:57:51.026 --> 00:57:53.063
I'm an attorney of law.

00:57:53.123 --> 00:57:57.166
I'm advising Mr. Paris on his claim to have for your estate.

00:57:57.226 --> 00:57:58.267
Why?

00:57:58.327 --> 00:58:04.799
You son of a bitch!

00:58:04.860 --> 00:58:12.251
Yes, he's a disgusting little man.

00:58:12.311 --> 00:58:15.082
I know, George Andrews.

00:58:15.142 --> 00:58:16.282
You do?

00:58:16.342 --> 00:58:17.333
Yes.

00:58:17.393 --> 00:58:21.634
In that case, you will understand why I'm so upset.

00:58:21.694 --> 00:58:23.955
You can't let that happen, Margaret.

00:58:24.015 --> 00:58:26.176
You cannot let that happen.

00:58:26.236 --> 00:58:28.226
Do you think I want it to happen?

00:58:28.286 --> 00:58:30.577
If you don't want it, don't allow it.

00:58:30.637 --> 00:58:33.292
It isn't as easy as that, Marie.

00:58:33.352 --> 00:58:35.639
We're in deep trouble.

00:58:35.699 --> 00:58:39.302
Henry owes money to this man a lot of money.

00:58:39.362 --> 00:58:41.965
Andrews can ruin us if he wants to.

00:58:42.025 --> 00:58:43.016
How?

00:58:43.076 --> 00:58:49.079
When he asked Henry for permission to speak to Laverne about marriage, Henry said no.

00:58:49.139 --> 00:58:58.740
So Andrews asked him to think again, and he said if Henry still said no, he was gonna ask for all the money that Henry owes him.

00:58:58.800 --> 00:59:00.132
How much does he owe him?

00:59:00.152 --> 00:59:01.373
$10,000.

00:59:01.393 --> 00:59:03.816
Oh my god.

00:59:03.877 --> 00:59:08.891
If we have to pay him, we'll have nothing.

00:59:08.951 --> 00:59:12.183
No house, no business, nothing.

00:59:12.243 --> 00:59:13.803
We'll be out on the street.

00:59:13.863 --> 00:59:15.184
Oh, Margaret.

00:59:15.244 --> 00:59:21.627
But if we agree to the marriage, Andrews will pay off all Henry's other debts as well.

00:59:21.688 --> 00:59:26.960
And he will also buy a useless piece of land that we own out near the Atchifu lion swamp.

00:59:27.020 --> 00:59:27.671
I see.

00:59:27.691 --> 00:59:31.453
I wish I could kill that man.

00:59:31.513 --> 00:59:33.924
But you know, that wouldn't help.

00:59:33.984 --> 00:59:36.998
He has three children by his first marriage.

00:59:37.058 --> 00:59:42.382
To be clear of the dead, I would have to kill all of them as well.

00:59:42.442 --> 00:59:45.254
You know what the best thing would be?

00:59:45.314 --> 00:59:46.885
What's that, Margaret?

00:59:46.945 --> 00:59:51.819
Have Laverne marry him, and then kill him.

00:59:51.879 --> 00:59:56.603
You know, that ain't such a bad idea.

00:59:56.663 --> 00:59:59.367
That's a crazy idea, Margaret, and you know it.

00:59:59.427 --> 01:00:00.380
Marie?

01:00:00.440 --> 01:00:01.490
Yes.

01:00:01.550 --> 01:00:04.111
Could you do that for me?

01:00:04.171 --> 01:00:05.582
What?

01:00:05.642 --> 01:00:07.482
Kill a man.

01:00:07.542 --> 01:00:09.833
Margaret, are you out of your mind?

01:00:09.894 --> 01:00:12.835
Don't be all surprised with me, Marie.

01:00:12.895 --> 01:00:15.086
I know about the things that you do.

01:00:15.146 --> 01:00:17.267
What are you talking about?

01:00:17.327 --> 01:00:19.898
What are you talking about?

01:00:19.958 --> 01:00:22.920
You know, darn well what I'm talking about, Marie.

01:00:22.980 --> 01:00:24.744
I know about you.

01:00:24.804 --> 01:00:29.270
and all those voodoo ceremonies down in Congo Square.

01:00:29.330 --> 01:00:30.522
Marie?

01:00:30.582 --> 01:00:31.864
Marie?

01:00:31.924 --> 01:00:33.424
Are you listening to me?

01:00:33.484 --> 01:00:34.305
I'm listening.

01:00:34.365 --> 01:00:35.726
Will you help me?

01:00:35.786 --> 01:00:40.120
Margaret, I don't normally work for white people.

01:00:40.180 --> 01:00:41.242
You don't, huh?

01:00:41.302 --> 01:00:43.734
Well, you're gonna start now.

01:00:43.794 --> 01:00:45.496
Okay, Margaret.

01:00:45.556 --> 01:00:47.074
I'll try to help.

01:00:47.134 --> 01:00:49.363
You know I'd do anything for you.

01:00:49.423 --> 01:00:50.103
And...

01:00:50.163 --> 01:00:51.324
And what?

01:00:51.384 --> 01:00:53.934
I just remembered something.

01:00:53.995 --> 01:00:59.397
Something that George Andrews said to me just before Jack died.

01:00:59.457 --> 01:01:08.270
Mrs. Paris, since the day of your marriage to Mr. Paris, he has been legally entitled to one half by your estate.

01:01:08.330 --> 01:01:11.022
I have an idea.

01:01:11.082 --> 01:01:15.138
I think I know what we can do.

01:01:15.198 --> 01:01:17.042
Mother.

01:01:17.102 --> 01:01:18.133
Laverne.

01:01:18.193 --> 01:01:21.114
Father just told me the most terrible thing.

01:01:21.134 --> 01:01:24.746
He wants me to marry Mr. Andrews.

01:01:24.806 --> 01:01:25.456
I know.

01:01:25.476 --> 01:01:26.937
I won't do it, Mother.

01:01:26.997 --> 01:01:31.099
I'd rather cut my own throat than let that man touch me.

01:01:31.159 --> 01:01:32.940
Laverne, calm down.

01:01:33.000 --> 01:01:33.820
Calm down.

01:01:33.840 --> 01:01:35.632
Calm down.

01:01:35.692 --> 01:01:37.832
Mother, I won't do it.

01:01:37.892 --> 01:01:43.298
I love you and I love Dad, but I will not marry that man.

01:01:43.358 --> 01:01:46.121
Thought of it makes me sick!

01:01:46.181 --> 01:01:47.702
Laverne, please.

01:01:47.762 --> 01:01:50.573
Just stop for a moment and listen to Marie.

01:01:50.633 --> 01:01:52.204
Listen to Marie.

01:01:52.264 --> 01:01:53.534
What for?

01:01:53.594 --> 01:01:55.166
Laverne.

01:01:55.226 --> 01:01:58.997
Just sit down for a moment and let me talk to you.

01:01:59.057 --> 01:02:00.618
I can help you.

01:02:00.678 --> 01:02:01.818
How?

01:02:01.879 --> 01:02:03.710
What can you do?

01:02:03.770 --> 01:02:05.930
If you marry this man.

01:02:05.990 --> 01:02:07.291
Marie, stop it.

01:02:07.351 --> 01:02:08.332
I don't want to hear it.

01:02:08.392 --> 01:02:09.182
Laverne.

01:02:09.242 --> 01:02:12.134
Quit squawking and hear me out.

01:02:12.194 --> 01:02:14.086
Sorry.

01:02:14.146 --> 01:02:18.617
When the fact is Laverne, you only have to marry him.

01:02:18.677 --> 01:02:24.279
Go through with the wedding, and you will immediately inherit half of his estate.

01:02:24.339 --> 01:02:25.039
And?

01:02:25.099 --> 01:02:26.450
And then, well...

01:02:26.510 --> 01:02:28.000
I'll tell him, Marie.

01:02:28.060 --> 01:02:32.302
If you don't marry Andrews, we lose everything.

01:02:32.362 --> 01:02:36.498
The house, the business, everything.

01:02:36.558 --> 01:02:39.483
And you won't tell me, Laverne.

01:02:39.543 --> 01:02:41.804
I didn't know about it until today either.

01:02:41.864 --> 01:02:44.696
Well, you two listened to my plan.

01:02:44.756 --> 01:02:46.107
Sorry.

01:02:46.167 --> 01:02:47.638
Laverne.

01:02:47.698 --> 01:02:55.562
As soon as you are married to Mr. Andrews, I will make sure that something happens to him.

01:02:55.622 --> 01:02:56.913
What?

01:02:56.973 --> 01:02:59.584
What's gonna happen to him?

01:02:59.645 --> 01:03:01.626
Trust me, Laverne.

01:03:01.686 --> 01:03:04.247
He won't be a problem for you.

01:03:04.307 --> 01:03:06.332
But I need your help.

01:03:06.392 --> 01:03:11.596
You must go to Mr. Andrew's house, and you must agree to marry him.

01:03:11.656 --> 01:03:12.546
Hurry!

01:03:12.606 --> 01:03:14.047
I can't do that!

01:03:14.067 --> 01:03:15.067
I ran!

01:03:15.107 --> 01:03:15.367
You can't!

01:03:15.387 --> 01:03:16.847
Hear me out!

01:03:16.907 --> 01:03:23.479
Agree to marry him, and bring me back something that belongs to him.

01:03:23.539 --> 01:03:25.369
What kind of thing?

01:03:25.429 --> 01:03:28.400
The simplest thing would be your handkerchief.

01:03:28.460 --> 01:03:33.152
Look, Margaret, I have to go now, but I'll be back later.

01:03:33.212 --> 01:03:35.253
Trust me, Laverne.

01:03:35.313 --> 01:03:37.794
Everything will be okay.

01:03:37.854 --> 01:03:41.065
Mama, why am I agreeing to this?

01:03:41.125 --> 01:03:44.676
I can't bear the idea of that man touching me.

01:03:44.696 --> 01:03:48.576
I deliver and trust Marie.

01:03:48.636 --> 01:03:50.717
She knows what she's doing.

01:03:50.777 --> 01:03:52.748
You'd better be right.

01:03:52.808 --> 01:03:59.902
Because if I have to live with that man, I'm gonna kill myself.

01:03:59.962 --> 01:04:07.458
At the next morning, Henry Salinger and his daughter Levern visited George Andrews.

01:04:07.518 --> 01:04:09.338
Henry!

01:04:09.399 --> 01:04:10.770
Hello, George.

01:04:10.830 --> 01:04:13.071
So good to see you.

01:04:13.091 --> 01:04:16.122
Hello, Mr. Andrews.

01:04:16.182 --> 01:04:20.986
Boy, Levern, you look good enough to eat.

01:04:21.046 --> 01:04:23.537
Can we come in, George?

01:04:23.597 --> 01:04:24.808
Sure thing, Henry.

01:04:24.868 --> 01:04:26.072
Come in.

01:04:26.132 --> 01:04:30.436
George, we've come to talk about your proposal.

01:04:30.496 --> 01:04:31.197
Good!

01:04:31.257 --> 01:04:37.769
And I hope you agree it's a good idea, because if you haven't, then it's the end of the road for the Salinger's.

01:04:37.789 --> 01:04:38.879
Ha ha ha ha!

01:04:38.939 --> 01:04:43.590
Well, yes, Laverne has agreed to marry you.

01:04:43.650 --> 01:04:44.999
Did you?

01:04:45.059 --> 01:04:49.052
Laverne, you just made the best decision of your life.

01:04:49.112 --> 01:04:50.094
Come here.

01:04:50.154 --> 01:04:51.595
Oh, Mr. Andrews.

01:04:51.655 --> 01:04:55.659
George, please, can we just discuss a few details?

01:04:55.719 --> 01:04:57.530
It's okay, Laverne.

01:04:57.591 --> 01:05:00.844
I can wait, but not for long.

01:05:00.904 --> 01:05:04.876
Let me get you folks a drink to celebrate.

01:05:04.936 --> 01:05:08.108
George, it's 11 o'clock in the morning.

01:05:08.168 --> 01:05:10.850
Isn't it kind of early to be drinking?

01:05:10.910 --> 01:05:13.512
Not when there's something like this to celebrate.

01:05:13.532 --> 01:05:14.933
No, George, I think...

01:05:14.953 --> 01:05:15.763
Oh, no, Dad.

01:05:15.823 --> 01:05:18.385
I think that's a nice idea.

01:05:18.445 --> 01:05:22.948
My father would like to join you, Mr. Andrews.

01:05:23.008 --> 01:05:29.122
Well, I'm glad she has more sense than you, Henry, even if she is just a woman.

01:05:29.142 --> 01:05:33.214
Hold on there, and I'll be back with some bourbon.

01:05:33.274 --> 01:05:34.993
Laverne.

01:05:35.053 --> 01:05:36.984
What are you thinking about?

01:05:37.044 --> 01:05:38.364
Don't worry, Dad.

01:05:38.424 --> 01:05:39.595
I know what I'm doing.

01:05:39.655 --> 01:05:41.675
You know that I don't drink in the morning.

01:05:41.735 --> 01:05:43.586
Well, you're gonna have to start, Dad.

01:05:43.606 --> 01:05:47.727
I want you to accept a glass of bourbon from Mr. Andrews.

01:05:47.787 --> 01:05:48.487
And then...

01:05:48.527 --> 01:05:49.548
Here we are!

01:05:49.608 --> 01:05:51.798
A bottle of my best bourbon.

01:05:51.859 --> 01:05:53.709
It's fifteen years old.

01:05:53.769 --> 01:05:57.890
Henry, have you any idea how much this stuff costs?

01:05:57.950 --> 01:05:58.921
No, George.

01:05:58.981 --> 01:06:00.841
I don't know how much it costs.

01:06:00.901 --> 01:06:03.705
Don't you want to know how much it costs?

01:06:03.765 --> 01:06:06.840
How much does it cost, George?

01:06:06.900 --> 01:06:09.743
This beauty is seven dollars a bottle.

01:06:09.803 --> 01:06:12.496
Seven dollars, but worth every cent.

01:06:12.556 --> 01:06:15.604
I have about sixty bottles of it in the cellar.

01:06:15.664 --> 01:06:17.959
Can I see the bottle, Mr. Andrews?

01:06:17.979 --> 01:06:20.659
Oh, why, yes, Laverne.

01:06:20.719 --> 01:06:21.750
Thank you.

01:06:21.810 --> 01:06:26.751
Well, Laverne, I didn't think you would be a bourbon drinker.

01:06:26.811 --> 01:06:28.322
Let me pour you a glass.

01:06:28.382 --> 01:06:29.222
Oh, no.

01:06:29.282 --> 01:06:31.522
I don't want to drink it, Mr. Andrews.

01:06:31.542 --> 01:06:35.483
I'm just interested in bottles.

01:06:35.503 --> 01:06:36.174
Oh!

01:06:36.234 --> 01:06:38.584
Careful.

01:06:38.644 --> 01:06:40.763
Laverne!

01:06:40.823 --> 01:06:42.234
Oh my God!

01:06:42.294 --> 01:06:44.745
That table is worth a fortune!

01:06:44.805 --> 01:06:47.306
I'm so sorry, Mr Andrews.

01:06:47.366 --> 01:06:49.236
Let me clear up the glass.

01:06:49.296 --> 01:06:51.147
Don't be ridiculous, Laverne.

01:06:51.207 --> 01:06:54.150
I have servants to do this kind of stuff.

01:06:54.210 --> 01:06:55.412
Martha!

01:06:55.472 --> 01:06:57.953
No, no, I broke it.

01:06:58.013 --> 01:06:59.253
I want to clear it up.

01:06:59.313 --> 01:07:00.743
No, no, Laverne, stop it.

01:07:00.803 --> 01:07:01.943
Get above the floor.

01:07:02.003 --> 01:07:03.934
It's okay, Mr. Andrews.

01:07:03.994 --> 01:07:06.274
Here, take this piece.

01:07:06.334 --> 01:07:07.264
Gah!

01:07:07.324 --> 01:07:09.115
Laverne, careful.

01:07:09.175 --> 01:07:11.405
You just cut Mr. Andrews hands.

01:07:11.465 --> 01:07:14.396
Jesus Christ, I'm bleeding to death.

01:07:14.456 --> 01:07:15.586
Martha!

01:07:15.646 --> 01:07:16.706
Oh, no.

01:07:16.766 --> 01:07:18.707
I'm so sorry.

01:07:18.767 --> 01:07:20.537
Quick, let me help you.

01:07:20.597 --> 01:07:24.538
Sit down here and give me a handkerchief.

01:07:24.598 --> 01:07:27.771
Oh, I'll use this one in your top pocket.

01:07:27.831 --> 01:07:30.413
Laverne, that's a silk handkerchief.

01:07:30.473 --> 01:07:31.804
It's okay, Dad.

01:07:31.864 --> 01:07:33.505
Mr. Andrews won't mind.

01:07:33.525 --> 01:07:35.557
Martha, where are you?

01:07:35.617 --> 01:07:38.059
I'm right here, Mr. Andrews.

01:07:38.119 --> 01:07:41.492
Oh my goodness, what have you done to your hand?

01:07:41.552 --> 01:07:43.324
What have I done to my hand?

01:07:43.384 --> 01:07:45.295
You can see with your own eyes.

01:07:45.355 --> 01:07:47.387
I'm bleeding to death.

01:07:47.447 --> 01:07:50.049
Come with me into the pantry, Mr. Andrews.

01:07:50.109 --> 01:07:51.310
I'll clean that up.

01:07:51.370 --> 01:07:57.706
Uh, we'll come back later, George, when things have calmed down a little.

01:07:57.766 --> 01:08:05.573
Later that day, Laverne took Mr. Andrew's silk handkerchief to Marie's house.

01:08:05.633 --> 01:08:07.725
I got this, Marie!

01:08:07.785 --> 01:08:09.702
Well done, Laverne.

01:08:09.762 --> 01:08:12.030
How come it's covered in blood?

01:08:12.090 --> 01:08:16.862
I dropped a seven dollar bottle of bourbon on a glass coffee table.

01:08:16.922 --> 01:08:18.933
There was glass everywhere.

01:08:18.993 --> 01:08:24.485
Then I accidentally cut Mr. Andrew's hand with a piece of broken glass.

01:08:24.545 --> 01:08:25.646
My.

01:08:25.706 --> 01:08:27.417
I really enjoyed it.

01:08:27.437 --> 01:08:30.308
Oh my God, what am I saying?

01:08:30.368 --> 01:08:31.958
I understand.

01:08:32.018 --> 01:08:33.789
What are you going to do with it?

01:08:33.849 --> 01:08:35.138
Look at this.

01:08:35.198 --> 01:08:36.716
The doll?

01:08:36.775 --> 01:08:38.127
What about it?

01:08:38.186 --> 01:08:42.239
Laverne, this is going to save your life.

01:08:42.299 --> 01:08:43.530
But it's...

01:08:43.590 --> 01:08:45.101
It's just a doll!

01:08:45.161 --> 01:08:45.992
Yes.

01:08:46.051 --> 01:08:50.214
And I'm going to put the handkerchief around the doll.

01:08:50.274 --> 01:08:52.416
Like this.

01:08:52.476 --> 01:08:54.647
And?

01:08:54.707 --> 01:08:57.519
How does that help anything?

01:08:57.579 --> 01:09:03.883
Laverne, it means I can do something to Mr. Andrews.

01:09:03.943 --> 01:09:05.978
Anytime I want.

01:09:06.038 --> 01:09:09.724
What do you mean, do something?

01:09:09.783 --> 01:09:11.235
Watch.

01:09:11.294 --> 01:09:19.168
First of all, I just put this needle into the doll, like this.

01:09:19.228 --> 01:09:28.302
And Mr. Andrews is gonna get a sharp paint, right there, in his chest.

01:09:28.362 --> 01:09:31.854
Martha, do you know where to?

01:09:31.914 --> 01:09:33.755
What's the matter, Mr. Andrews?

01:09:33.775 --> 01:09:36.022
Nothing.

01:09:36.082 --> 01:09:39.001
You're okay.

01:09:39.061 --> 01:09:40.772
Sit down for a moment.

01:09:40.833 --> 01:09:44.657
I've just got a pain here in my chest.

01:09:44.717 --> 01:09:46.409
It's okay.

01:09:46.469 --> 01:09:47.480
It's gone now.

01:09:47.540 --> 01:09:52.736
Mr. Andrews, when are you going to take my advice and stop drinking so much bourbon?

01:09:52.796 --> 01:09:54.678
Never, Martha, never.

01:09:54.738 --> 01:10:06.239
I'll let bourbon too much to ever stop.

01:10:06.299 --> 01:10:18.490
A few weeks later, the wedding took place.

01:10:18.550 --> 01:10:23.684
After the church service, there was a big party in Andrews' house in Canal Street.

01:10:23.744 --> 01:10:27.838
Laverne was sick with worry.

01:10:27.898 --> 01:10:32.320
Congratulations, Laverne, and good luck.

01:10:32.380 --> 01:10:33.702
Thanks.

01:10:33.762 --> 01:10:38.975
My God, she needs all the luck she can get.

01:10:39.035 --> 01:10:41.357
Hello, Marie.

01:10:41.417 --> 01:10:42.966
Hi, Margaret.

01:10:43.026 --> 01:10:44.426
How are you feeling?

01:10:44.486 --> 01:10:47.838
Terrible, but there is some good news.

01:10:47.898 --> 01:10:52.693
Andrews has already paid off Henry's debts to all the banks in town.

01:10:52.753 --> 01:10:53.713
That's wonderful.

01:10:53.773 --> 01:10:56.045
Marie, I'll have earned.

01:10:56.105 --> 01:10:57.246
You look lovely.

01:10:57.306 --> 01:10:59.148
Marie, what's going on?

01:10:59.208 --> 01:11:01.660
You said everything would be okay.

01:11:01.720 --> 01:11:04.102
Well, it doesn't feel okay to me.

01:11:04.122 --> 01:11:05.533
Don't panic.

01:11:05.593 --> 01:11:09.004
It would be okay, I promise.

01:11:09.064 --> 01:11:16.166
Ladies and gentlemen, please raise your glasses for a toast to George and Laverne.

01:11:16.226 --> 01:11:22.850
George and Laverne!

01:11:22.910 --> 01:11:28.713
Marie, are you...

01:11:28.772 --> 01:11:30.864
Oh, where's Marie?

01:11:30.924 --> 01:11:32.535
Laverne, did you see where Marie went?

01:11:32.595 --> 01:11:33.776
No.

01:11:33.836 --> 01:11:38.614
No one knew where Marie was, but she was nearby.

01:11:38.674 --> 01:11:47.380
and she had the doll covered with a blood-stained silkenkerchief, and she had a sharp needle.

01:11:47.439 --> 01:12:02.129
Now, ladies and gentlemen, pray silence for the groom, Mr. George Andrews.

01:12:02.189 --> 01:12:06.885
Thank you.

01:12:06.945 --> 01:12:08.156
Thank you very much.

01:12:08.216 --> 01:12:15.168
Well, I'm so glad that you could all come to my wedding, and I hope the food and drink are to your satisfaction.

01:12:15.228 --> 01:12:16.648
Well, they should be.

01:12:16.708 --> 01:12:23.380
This whole thing costs me a huge pile of money.

01:12:23.440 --> 01:12:30.622
And let's be honest, money is what this is all about.

01:12:30.682 --> 01:12:33.354
I was caught all my life.

01:12:33.414 --> 01:12:35.166
I made a lot of money.

01:12:35.226 --> 01:12:37.598
I mean a lot of money.

01:12:37.658 --> 01:12:39.890
And now I get my reward.

01:12:39.950 --> 01:12:42.642
I had a beautiful young bride and...

01:12:42.682 --> 01:12:46.225
Dumb by loud we do.

01:12:46.285 --> 01:12:48.396
What was that?

01:12:48.456 --> 01:12:50.278
What was what, George?

01:12:50.338 --> 01:12:53.000
Voice, Candace, spooky voice.

01:12:53.060 --> 01:12:55.621
Dumb by loud.

01:12:55.681 --> 01:12:57.290
Dead is again.

01:12:57.350 --> 01:12:58.702
Didn't anyone hear it?

01:12:58.762 --> 01:13:00.232
No, no, no.

01:13:00.292 --> 01:13:02.924
No George, no one heard anything.

01:13:02.984 --> 01:13:04.555
You didn't hear a voice?

01:13:04.615 --> 01:13:06.566
Saying something foreign?

01:13:06.626 --> 01:13:11.629
No George, the only voice we can hear is yours.

01:13:11.689 --> 01:13:18.253
Right, well, as I was saying, I have a beautiful young bride.

01:13:18.313 --> 01:13:22.504
Don't find out we don't...

01:13:22.564 --> 01:13:25.403
George, you're right.

01:13:25.463 --> 01:13:27.374
Of course I'm all right.

01:13:27.434 --> 01:13:28.555
It's my wedding day.

01:13:28.615 --> 01:13:31.236
What was I saying?

01:13:31.296 --> 01:13:34.938
I have always believed that what you...

01:13:34.998 --> 01:13:39.031
You get what you do.

01:13:39.071 --> 01:13:40.391
George, sit down, man.

01:13:40.411 --> 01:13:41.342
You look terrible.

01:13:41.402 --> 01:13:43.003
Leave me alone, damn you.

01:13:43.063 --> 01:13:47.013
This is my wedding party, which I have paid for.

01:13:47.073 --> 01:13:51.763
Most people would expect the brides far to pay for all this, but he didn't.

01:13:51.823 --> 01:14:00.978
Get out of the way!

01:14:01.038 --> 01:14:04.240
Let him get some air!

01:14:04.300 --> 01:14:07.502
Get some stuff!

01:14:07.562 --> 01:14:10.382
Charles was dead.

01:14:10.442 --> 01:14:13.344
The doctors said he had a heart attack.

01:14:13.404 --> 01:14:17.212
Oliver was a widow before her wedding day was over.

01:14:17.272 --> 01:14:23.456
But I guess inherent in a hundred thousand dollars of charges money helped her to recover quickly.

01:14:23.516 --> 01:14:30.136
And Marie, well, she was most definitely the Queen of New Orleans.

